#: src/introduction.md:1
msgid "deck"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:3
msgid "**One slide is one complete HTML document.**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:5
msgid ""
"`deck` is a local slide runtime and development environment written in Rust. "
"A slide is a file you can read, diff and review — plain HTML, CSS and "
"JavaScript. There is no slide DSL, no required Markdown, and no slide body "
"hidden inside TOML or JSON."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:11
msgid ""
"New here? Read [Install and create a deck](./getting-started.md), then "
"[Writing a slide](./writing-slides.md). Everything else is reference "
"material you can come back to."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:17
msgid "See it running"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:19
msgid ""
"The [introduction deck](/deck/slide/present) is itself a deck, built by "
"`deck build` and published next to this guide. Its source lives in "
"[`site/`](https://github.com/azishio/deck/tree/main/site) if you want to "
"read a real deck rather than snippets."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:23
msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:27
msgid "**Directory-based discovery**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:27
msgid "`slides/**/*.html` in lexicographic order. No slide list to maintain."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:28
msgid "**iframe isolation**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:28
msgid ""
"Per-slide JavaScript, CSS and DOM state, with a three-frame ring so 100 "
"slides do not mean 100 iframes."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:29
msgid "**Absolute steps**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:29
msgid ""
"`screen state = f(slide_id, step)`. Deep links and reloads land exactly "
"where you left off."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:30
msgid "**Tailwind CSS**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:30
msgid ""
"v4 browser build, vendored. Utilities compile inside each slide — no "
"bundler, no CDN."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:31
msgid "**Anime.js**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:31
msgid "Vendored and importable straight from a slide."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:32
msgid "**Hot reload**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:32
msgid ""
"HTML, CSS and component edits apply while keeping the current slide, step "
"and presenter timer."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:33
msgid "**Presenter View**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:33
msgid ""
"Current and next slide, speaker notes, timer, clock, blackout, live "
"diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid "**Printing**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid ""
"A real `/print` page for the browser's own print dialog. The CLI never "
"generates a PDF."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:35
msgid "**Checks**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:35
msgid ""
"headless Chromium finds layout, runtime and asset problems. Human, JSON or "
"SARIF output."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:36
msgid "**Static build**"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:36
msgid "`deck build` emits a folder any static host can serve."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:38
msgid "Why plain HTML"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:40
msgid ""
"Most slide tools ask you to learn their format. This one asks you to use the "
"web platform you already know."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:43
msgid ""
"**Editable by humans and agents alike.** No intermediate representation to "
"translate through, so \"add a slide about X\" is a request an agent can "
"carry out and you can review as a diff."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:46
msgid ""
"**Nothing is off-limits.** SVG, Canvas, WebGL, a live iframe, a custom "
"element you wrote this morning — if it runs in Chromium, it runs in a slide."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:48
msgid ""
"**Isolated by construction.** One slide's JavaScript cannot leak into the "
"next, so a broken experiment on slide 12 does not take down slide 13."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:50
msgid ""
"**Verifiable.** Overflow, clipped text, broken assets and console errors are "
"lint rules, not things you discover from the back of the room."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:53
msgid "What it is not"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:55
msgid ""
"`deck` targets **Chromium-based browsers only**, on purpose. The `iframe` "
"boundary isolates DOM, CSS and JavaScript state; it is **not** a security "
"sandbox, and slide HTML is treated as trusted local code. Running untrusted "
"decks is out of scope."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:59
msgid ""
"The CLI never produces a PDF. Printing belongs to the browser, and `/print` "
"is a real page you can inspect before committing to paper."
msgstr ""

